From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ampheck <support@ampheck.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Nov 2026 22:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: boot_mode: enter RockUSB for loader reboot

Upstream U-Boot handles fastboot and UMS reboot modes but ignores
BOOT_LOADER.  Linux writes BOOT_LOADER for `reboot loader`, so the mode
gets cleared and the board continues to boot normally.

Run the RockUSB command through preboot for BOOT_LOADER, matching the
existing fastboot/UMS handling.  The board defconfig enables the USB
gadget, RockUSB function and preboot command execution.

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
index ba3e22618e3..27da64599da 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
@@ -95,6 +95,10 @@ int setup_boot_mode(void)
 	writel(BOOT_NORMAL, reg);
 
 	switch (boot_mode) {
+	case BOOT_LOADER:
+		debug("%s: enter rockusb!\n", __func__);
+		env_set("preboot", "setenv preboot; rockusb 0 mmc 0");
+		break;
 	case BOOT_FASTBOOT:
 		debug("%s: enter fastboot!\n", __func__);
 		env_set("preboot", "setenv preboot; fastboot usb 0");
-- 
